JSON Schema patterns commonly use ECMAScript shorthand character
classes. Expand supported shorthand classes into GBNF character classes
instead of falling back to an unconstrained string when parsing them.

Upstream: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27580

diff --git a/common/json-schema-to-grammar.cpp b/common/json-schema-to-grammar.cpp
--- a/common/json-schema-to-grammar.cpp
+++ b/common/json-schema-to-grammar.cpp
@@ -282,6 +282,31 @@
 static std::unordered_set<char> NON_LITERAL_SET = {'|', '.', '(', ')', '[', ']', '{', '}', '*', '+', '?', '^', '$'};
